# gen_fu_pmp_lock_promotion: two bins leave bins_not_hit because the sampler that excluded them is gone

WHAT THIS CLAIMS. gen_pmp_addr_write_cg.cr_self_lock.locked_rlb1_written and
gen_pmp_addr_write_cg.cr_tor_lock.nl_tor_rlb1_written are hit at every one of the 40 measured seeds
of gen_test_pmp_lock in the step-1b block, so they become declared bins. NOT claimed: anything about
the other two PMP entries, which this touch leaves byte-identical, or about any bin outside those two.

WHY THEY WERE EXCLUDED AND WHY THAT ENDED. Both reasons were declaration-class and said the sampler
sets the lock field from the entry's lock bit AND NOT mseccfg.RLB, making locked and rlb1 mutually
exclusive by construction so no stimulus could reach the cross. That was true of the sampler as it
stood. The step-1b sampler fixes took the raw lock bit, so the exclusion is gone and the stimulus
this entry already had reaches both bins. Pinned to commits, because a bare line number moves:

  at 4cd3ff6, the commit the block is pinned to
    gen_fcov_pkg.sv:2448  bit self_locked = pmp_cfg_pre[i][7];
    gen_fcov_pkg.sv:2464  next_locked = pmp_cfg_pre[i+1][7];
  at 9a42c17ee69316dbc68b1536d5e9abe148078941, this touch's base
    gen_fcov_pkg.sv:2506  bit self_locked = pmp_cfg_pre[i][7];
    gen_fcov_pkg.sv:2522  next_locked = pmp_cfg_pre[i+1][7];

Neither carries an RLB term. So the reasons described a sampler that no longer exists, which makes
them false claims about the entry's runs rather than merely stale ones, and they are removed rather
than reworded.

THE MEASUREMENT, from the retained block's own artifacts.
  block            dv/auto_dv/evidence/gen_pmp_measurement/gen_index.md, gen_pmp_1b.yaml,
                   gen_pmp_1b_bins.txt, retained at 2956a8a, measured on 4cd3ff6
  read by          each run's own urgReport_variable_form/grpinfo.txt, parsed with the reviewed
                   gen_read_keyed.parse_report, a bin counting as hit when its count is non-zero
  gen_test_pmp_lock            40 runs, 40 PASS, 39 declared bins all hit at every seed
    locked_rlb1_written        40 of 40
    nl_tor_rlb1_written        40 of 40
  gen_test_pmp_csr_warl        39 runs, 39 PASS, 179 declared bins all hit at every seed
  gen_test_pmp_mseccfg         40 runs, 40 PASS,  26 declared bins all hit at every seed

THE csr_warl DENOMINATOR IS 39 OF 40, not 40, and it is a property of the pinned commit rather than
of the entry today: seed 230969025 produces no program at 4cd3ff6, whose WARL generator asserts on
its own draw. The backstop that closes that hole is committed at 4017573, after the block's pin. No
fortieth run was spliced in from a different generator, which would have put two generators in one
seed set.

csr_warl IS UNCHANGED OVER ALL 81 OF ITS not_hit LINES, checked rather than assumed: 78
seed-dependent, 2 stimulus, 1 declaration; none is hit at every seed, 78 are hit at some and 3 at
none. Every one of the 78 seed-dependent reasons carries its own count, and every one of those counts
equals its measured value with the denominator 39 before and after. That includes the line the DV
Lead asked to be re-checked, cr_rw01_mml.rw01_mml1_l1_rlb1_stored, which records 16 of the entry's 39
measured seeds and measures 16 of 39. So the step-1b fixes moved nothing in that entry's
seed-dependent set.

A TOOL DEFECT THIS MEASUREMENT PASSED THROUGH, recorded because the first reading was wrong and the
wrong reading was reported. My census matched the not_hit class token with a pattern that cannot
contain a hyphen, so "seed-dependent" never matched and 78 of the 81 lines were dropped SILENTLY: the
entry read as having three not_hit lines and I reported that figure. It was the second such parse
defect in one day, after MISSING-FROM-REPORT in a run-report census. The remedy is not vigilance
about hyphens: both censuses now count the raw marker lines and ASSERT the match count equals it, so
a token that widens again fails loudly instead of shrinking the input.

WHAT THE RE-RENDER PRODUCES, run in place and checked entry by entry:
  gen_test_pmp_lock       39 declared, 2 not_hit  ->  41 declared, 0 not_hit   (this touch)
  gen_test_pmp_csr_warl   179 declared, 81 not_hit  ->  byte-identical
  gen_test_pmp_mseccfg     26 declared,  0 not_hit  ->  byte-identical
The promoted entry is 19 coverpoint bins and 22 cross bins. No plan change is needed: the plan
already traces both bins to their items, and it was the test's own bins_not_hit that excluded them.
gen_test_lib --self-test exits 0 on a detached archive carrying the changed test and manifest, which
is the rule that the manifest and declare_bins agree.
